A||N||6||Vlad||Very slow cranking when engine hot.||||4||
Z||000000||Vlad||09-05-2000||07:48 PM||||Hello<P>V6 engine starts fantastic when it's cold; however, when it is in normal operating temp, the cranking is VERY slow. Like having a battery that about to die. I think this is a heat related problem.<P>Any idea?<P>||||reg||4
Z||000001||theogre||09-05-2000||08:30 PM||||Heat soaked starter or a bad battery cable would do it. Obviously you want to have the battery checked first. Make sure it's hot when you check it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||09-05-2000||11:37 PM||||I concur with the wise Ogre. Starter is most likely the problem!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Vlad||09-06-2000||12:19 AM||||Thanks for ideas.<P>But what should I look for once I'm going to check battery and starter? <BR>What should I expect to find? <BR>And how to fix whatever I will find there...:-/.....?<P>Sorry about so many questions at once...<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||gtsonly||09-06-2000||06:21 AM||||my experience with a mustang with the same problem turned out to be a timing issue. i had the timing so advance when it was warm it acted like you discribe. fixed the timing and all went away. <P>  my two cents!!<BR>   chris hatch<BR>   1986.5 gt with t-tops||||reg||6
Z||000005||Alex4mula||09-06-2000||08:14 AM||||Had exactly the same problem. Usually is the selenoid but it cost half of a new starter. I bought the whole thing and probem was gone.||||reg||1
Z||000006||pollock||09-06-2000||09:52 AM||||I had the same prob as gtsonly, on my Mustang.  I'd check the timing before you bought any new stuff.||||reg||1
